# The Docker build context is THIS directory (Railway's service Root Directory),
# so Docker reads this file — not the repo-root .dockerignore, which is never
# consulted for a backend/ context. Without this, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile
# sweeps in backend/.env — live LLM keys, the Supabase service key and the DB
# password — and bakes them into an image layer, where they survive even if a
# later layer deletes the file.
#
# Railway builds from the git repo, so .gitignore already keeps .env out of ITS
# context. This is what protects a local `docker build`, which reads the working
# tree and does not consult .gitignore at all.

**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Secrets / credentials
*.pem
*.key
**/service-account*.json

# Python build/cache noise — reinstalled in the image, and copying it
# invalidates the layer cache on every change.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/*.egg-info
**/.venv
**/venv

# Local noise
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log
**/coverage
**/htmlcov

# NOTE: README.md must NOT be ignored — pyproject.toml declares
# `readme = "README.md"`, so the editable install fails without it.
